<%# locals: login:

    What Prism is doing to this repository right now, in two sentences, for
    the menu behind the "Watching" button.

    **Paired with `_consent`, which says the same things at length.** That one
    is asked before anything happens — "do you want this?" — and has room for
    three paragraphs. This one answers "what is happening?" for someone who
    already said yes, so it is present tense and short. Two partials rather
    than one because the prose genuinely differs; the facts must not.

    Neither may lose a fact: what Prism writes and on which pull requests,
    whose account GitHub records it under, and how to call it off.
    test/views/webhook_subscriptions/consent_copy_test.rb asserts that of
    both, so dropping one here fails rather than quietly disagreeing with
    the other. %>
Adds a review link to the description of new pull requests that change Markdown,
as <span class="font-medium text-brand">@<%= login %></span>.
Delete the link from a pull request and Prism leaves that one alone.
